From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HeavyGee <gc@lockhouse.systems>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(soup): reinstate the Garden/XR entry chip in the sessions toolbar

feat/garden-route placed <GardenXrEntryChip /> inline in the sessions
header in web/src/router.tsx, beside the session count. Upstream has since
moved that whole header into <SessionList renderHeader toolbarExtras={[...]}>,
so the layer merge takes the base for that region — otherwise the composed
tip would render a second header the base no longer renders.

That leaves the chip with nowhere to live, so it is reinstated here as a
toolbarExtras entry (id 'garden-xr', keep 4) alongside browse and settings.

A heal rather than part of the merge resolution: toolbarExtras is outside
the conflict region, git treated it as context, and rerere replays
conflicted regions only — so a hand edit there is silently dropped by the
next compose, and in full-recipe mode every run recomposes from the base.

diff --git a/web/src/router.tsx b/web/src/router.tsx
--- a/web/src/router.tsx
+++ b/web/src/router.tsx
@@ -345,6 +345,16 @@
                                 )
                             }] : []),
                             {
+                                // Garden/XR entry (fork). It used to sit inline
+                                // beside the session count; upstream moved that
+                                // header into <SessionList renderHeader>, so the
+                                // chip belongs in the toolbar rather than in a
+                                // header this file no longer renders.
+                                id: 'garden-xr',
+                                keep: 4,
+                                node: <GardenXrEntryChip />
+                            },
+                            {
                                 id: 'settings',
                                 keep: 6,
                                 node: (
-- 
